IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`

-- g3-fixtures.l4: named cases for the tests of group G3.  No assertion lives here.  The facts of each case are chosen from the text of Articles 8 to 10, and
-- the expected values in the tests are decided from the SOURCE before the code is run (the brief's rule for tests).

§ `Fixtures for the tests of Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `People, entities and the register records`

`Ann Le Brun` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Ann Le Brun"
        `is a natural person` IS TRUE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

`Bob Renouf` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Bob Renouf"
        `is a natural person` IS TRUE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

`Jersey Trustees Limited` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Jersey Trustees Limited"
        `is a natural person` IS FALSE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS TRUE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity called` nm `standing as` st `and falling within` ks MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS nm
        `standing on the register` IS st
        `kinds of entity` IS ks
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS LIST `Ann Le Brun`, `Bob Renouf`
        purposes IS EMPTY

GIVEN e IS AN Entity
      registered IS A DATE
      deregistered IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`the register record of` e `registered on` registered `and deregistered on` deregistered MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS e
        `registration number` IS "C-0001"
        `registered name` IS e's name
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS registered
        `date deregistered` IS deregistered
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the relief of poverty"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Food parcels are given to those in need in Jersey, and the charity checks need before it gives"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

`a company in the general section` MEANS `an entity called` "Alpha Charity Limited" `standing as` `entered in the general section` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)
`a company in the restricted section` MEANS `an entity called` "Alpha Charity Limited" `standing as` `entered in the restricted section` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)
`a company, formerly registered` MEANS `an entity called` "Alpha Charity Limited" `standing as` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)
`a company that applies` MEANS `an entity called` "Alpha Charity Limited" `standing as` `an applicant for registration` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)

`Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` MEANS `the register record of` `a company in the general section` `registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and deregistered on` NOTHING
`Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` MEANS `the register record of` `a company in the restricted section` `registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and deregistered on` NOTHING
`Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` MEANS `the register record of` `a company, formerly registered` `registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and deregistered on` (JUST (YMD 2024 6 1))

`no further facts for Article 8(3)` MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS EMPTY
        `principal address entered` IS NOTHING
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS EMPTY

GIVEN s IS A `Section of the register`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
`a placement in` s `on` d MEANS
    `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` WITH
        `the section` IS s
        `date of the entry` IS d

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity falling within` ks MEANS `an entity called` "Test Entity" `standing as` `entered in the general section` `and falling within` ks

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`a charity registered on` d MEANS `the register record of` `a company in the general section` `registered on` d `and deregistered on` NOTHING

§§ `The readings: the favoured interpretation and one interpretation per other reading`

`the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
        `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
        `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
        `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
        `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
        `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
        `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
        `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
        `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
        `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
        `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
        `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
        `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
        `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

-- F3.1: the other reading (B): from the day the charity is deregistered

`interpretation F3.1 reading B` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
        `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the charity is deregistered`
